The corrected screen closes the major residual family. Three low-symmetry WO₃ models dominate: P\(\bar1\) COD 2106293 (Rwp 8.15%), monoclinic P2₁/c COD 2311041 (8.21%), and an older monoclinic model COD 1528915 (8.89%), each at about 18.5 wt%. The triclinic gain over P2₁/c is only 0.06 percentage point and uses three extra lattice freedoms; I’m carrying both forward but nominating the room-temperature monoclinic P2₁/c neutron structure as the chemically economical model. Tetragonal, orthorhombic, and hexagonal branches are much worse or collapse.

Phase closure adds a third phase cleanly: wurtzite ZnO lowers Rwp from 8.21% to 6.57% with a stable ~4.8 wt% contribution and only 0.24–0.36% cell expansion. Rocksalt and zincblende ZnO both collapse below 0.2 wt%. The inventory is therefore ZnWO₄ + monoclinic WO₃ + wurtzite ZnO; I’m now refining that three-phase model and checking that no coherent residual family remains.

